  "limitations": [
    "Four tiny independent Java-written/read PNGs: 5x5 grayscale16 Adam7, 3x3 RGBA8 Adam7, and 3x2 RGB transparency/suggested-palette images in Adam7 and noninterlaced forms. This is not all dimensions/filter combinations or comprehensive PNG conformance.",
    "Indexed, grayscale-alpha/gray tRNS, packed low-bit grayscale, RGB/RGBA16, APNG, ICC/HDR and unconnected color-profile semantics still refuse. The original native map compiler also rejects indexed and noncanonical RGB map depths; sources are not silently converted to bypass it.",
    "The 16 MiB decoded limit is admission, not a measured peak-heap guarantee. Inflation and output buffers coexist; compressed input is bounded at 8 MiB and pixels at 4,194,304. Oversized-header refusal is checked without generating a large image.",
    "The actual decoder, Wasm image bridge and worker snapshot inspection run under Node with the existing separate 20-type fixture and a controlled VM/Worker host. No real browser worker, GPU, GC or performance qualification is claimed.",
    "The existing image-map smoke was adjusted to reject invalid interlace method 2; valid Adam7 is now connected. Its earlier broad scoped cases were not rerun in this batch.",
    "Full image-map options and categorical dimension applications, native terrain stages, hydrology, custom registry, durable persistence, assets and dependency/release qualification remain unfinished."
  ],
